# Perception data pipeline

Full contract: `docs/architecture/sensor_data_pipeline.md`.

Single-stream adapters may canonicalize one topic. Only the preprocessor
pairs streams, keeps history, corrects frames, and scores motion.

Downstream nodes subscribe to `/luggage/preprocessed/...`. They do not
subscribe to raw D435 / Mid-360 / joints to invent alignment.
`SyncedObservation` is internal to the preprocessor, not a ROS message.

## Must

- Do not hand-roll tolerance pairing (`message_filters` slop, "latest RGB +
  latest cloud") in a consumer. Exact-join identical stamps is allowed.
- A single-input consumer may cache one preprocessed message and reject it
  by age against `primary_stamp`.
- Every per-stream struct carries its own `stamp`. `DepthFrame` also carries
  `units`; clouds carry `data_frame` separately from `frame_id`.
- Pick detection is camera-triggered. Never block until lidar is present.
- Tolerate an absent lidar stream.

## Missing data is flagged, not faked

```python
# BAD
obs.lidar_points = np.empty((0, 3))

# GOOD
obs.lidar_points = None
obs.flags.lidar_ok = False
```

## Buffers

Bounded ring buffers, pruned by stamp. Unbounded queues are a defect.

| Stream | Retain |
|---|---|
| RGB / depth / camera points | 5-10 frames |
| Lidar scans | 2-4 scans |
| Lidar IMU, `joint_states` | 0.5-1 s |
